        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a6a6123e-9d75-5e9a-b658-a1026d633a78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Amesiella, Cucurbita\n- Places: Luzon, Philippines, Andes, Mesoamerica\n- People: Oakes Ames\n- Organizations: Harvard University\n- Concepts: orchids, gourds, Cucurbitaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Oakes Ames lived from 1874 to 1950 and founded the orchid herbarium at Harvard University.\n- Amesiella is a genus of orchids endemic to the island of Luzon in the Philippines.\n- Amesiella is named for Oakes Ames.\n- Cucurbita is a genus of herbaceous vines in the gourd family Cucurbitaceae.\n- Cucurbita is also known as cucurbits.\n- Cucurbita is native to the Andes and Mesoamerica.\n- The Latin meaning of Cucurbita is gourd.",
